.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/dlv Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "`dlv(obj, keypath)` [![NPM](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dlv.svg)](https://npmjs.com/package/dlv) [![Build](https://travis-ci.org/developit/dlv.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/developit/dlv)"
.PP
.RS 4
Safely get a dot-notated path within a nested object, with ability to return a default if the full key path does not exist or the value is undefined 
.RE
.PP
.SS "Why?"
Smallest possible implementation: only \fB130 bytes\&.\fP

.PP
You could write this yourself, but then you'd have to write \fRtests\fP\&.

.PP
Supports ES Modules, CommonJS and globals\&.
.SS "Installation"
\fRnpm install --save dlv\fP
.SS "Usage"
\fRdelve(object, keypath, [default])\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
import delve from 'dlv';

let obj = {
    a: {
        b: {
            c: 1,
            d: undefined,
            e: null
        }
    }
};

//use string dot notation for keys
delve(obj, 'a\&.b\&.c') === 1;

//or use an array key
delve(obj, ['a', 'b', 'c']) === 1;

delve(obj, 'a\&.b') === obj\&.a\&.b;

//returns undefined if the full key path does not exist and no default is specified
delve(obj, 'a\&.b\&.f') === undefined;

//optional third parameter for default if the full key in path is missing
delve(obj, 'a\&.b\&.f', 'foo') === 'foo';

//or if the key exists but the value is undefined
delve(obj, 'a\&.b\&.d', 'foo') === 'foo';

//Non\-truthy defined values are still returned if they exist at the full keypath
delve(obj, 'a\&.b\&.e', 'foo') === null;

//undefined obj or key returns undefined, unless a default is supplied
delve(undefined, 'a\&.b\&.c') === undefined;
delve(undefined, 'a\&.b\&.c', 'foo') === 'foo';
delve(obj, undefined, 'foo') === 'foo';
.fi
.PP
.SS "Setter Counterparts"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdset\fP by \fR@lukeed\fP is the spiritual "set" counterpart of \fRdlv\fP and very fast\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRbury\fP by \fR@kalmbach\fP does the opposite of \fRdlv\fP and is implemented in a very similar manner\&.
.PP
